---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";

const contentTitle = "Cookie Policy";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={contentTitle}
  description="This site sets no cookies and collects nothing about you."
  type="website"
>
  <Header
    title={contentTitle}
    subtitle="Come to the dark side, we have cookies!"
  />

  <div class="max-w-bulma mx-auto w-full px-6 py-12">
    <div class="prose mx-auto">
      <p>
        Actually, we don&#39;t. <b>This site sets no cookies at all</b>, runs no
        analytics, and has no third-party embeds, trackers or advertising. There
        is nothing to opt into and nothing to opt out of.
      </p>
      <p>
        The one thing stored on your device is a single
        <code>localStorage</code> entry named <code>theme</code>, which
        remembers whether you chose the light or dark colour scheme. It never
        leaves your browser, it is not a cookie, and it is not sent with any
        request. If you never touch the theme toggle, even that is not written —
        the site simply follows your operating system preference.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is a set of static files with no server-side logic and no
        database. Clearing your browser data for this domain removes the theme
        preference and returns everything to its default.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pages are served by Cloudflare, which processes request metadata such as
        IP addresses in order to deliver them, as described in the <a
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
          >Cloudflare privacy policy</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        Links to external sites — GitHub, LinkedIn, Mastodon and the rest — are
        plain links. Those sites have their own policies, which apply once you
        follow them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
